WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.184 --> 00:00:04.017
- Hello Believe Nation.

00:00:04.017 --> 00:00:05.549
Today we're going to
look at the seven things

00:00:05.549 --> 00:00:08.441
you should do before quitting your job.

00:00:08.441 --> 00:00:10.058
And as always guys, if you hear a point

00:00:10.058 --> 00:00:11.157
that really resonates with you

00:00:11.157 --> 00:00:13.081
please leave it down
in the comments below.

00:00:13.081 --> 00:00:14.405
Put quotes around it so other people

00:00:14.405 --> 00:00:15.678
can be inspired as well.

00:00:15.678 --> 00:00:18.007
And also writing it down
helps you lock it in

00:00:18.007 --> 00:00:19.032
for yourself too.

00:00:19.032 --> 00:00:19.865
Enjoy.

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:26.577
(electronic music)

00:00:28.352 --> 00:00:29.440
So I've always been an advocate

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:31.073
of you don't need to quit your job

00:00:31.073 --> 00:00:32.820
and go into your business full time.

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:35.144
I've always been a fan
of doing it on the side

00:00:35.144 --> 00:00:36.442
and then eventually getting to the point

00:00:36.442 --> 00:00:37.853
where you can quit your job.

00:00:37.853 --> 00:00:39.757
And then go full time on your company.

00:00:39.757 --> 00:00:41.724
And here are my seven things

00:00:41.724 --> 00:00:45.671
that you should look at before
you take that leap full time.

00:00:45.671 --> 00:00:48.171
(hiphop beat)

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:51.686
Number one is think
about taking another job.

00:00:51.686 --> 00:00:53.109
This might sound a little counterintuitive

00:00:53.109 --> 00:00:54.886
because we're talking
about quitting our job

00:00:54.886 --> 00:00:55.980
and going full time.

00:00:55.980 --> 00:00:58.165
The reason to have a job is to learn.

00:00:58.165 --> 00:01:00.591
The reason to have a job
is to make an income right?

00:01:00.591 --> 00:01:02.700
You're paying off your
bills and you're learning.

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:05.018
And so I'll be looking at
my current job right now.

00:01:05.018 --> 00:01:05.851
If you're not making enough

00:01:05.851 --> 00:01:07.027
from your own business to quit

00:01:07.027 --> 00:01:07.860
and you need to have a job

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:10.684
then are you learning
enough in the business

00:01:10.684 --> 00:01:12.257
that you're in right now?

00:01:12.257 --> 00:01:13.586
Are you learning the skills that

00:01:13.586 --> 00:01:15.433
are going to help you
with your own company?

00:01:15.433 --> 00:01:16.702
If not, then I'd be looking

00:01:16.702 --> 00:01:19.155
at how do I get those
skills somewhere else?

00:01:19.155 --> 00:01:20.306
How do I quit my job?

00:01:20.306 --> 00:01:23.046
And before going all into my business

00:01:23.046 --> 00:01:25.430
I have a bridge step at another company

00:01:25.430 --> 00:01:26.709
where I'm going to learn.

00:01:26.709 --> 00:01:29.244
When your growing up, you pay
to get a University education.

00:01:29.244 --> 00:01:31.887
Here you are getting paid to get educated.

00:01:31.887 --> 00:01:33.361
You're getting paid to make mistakes.

00:01:33.361 --> 00:01:36.019
You're getting paid to make
contacts in the industry.

00:01:36.019 --> 00:01:37.317
And so I'd be looking at a company

00:01:37.317 --> 00:01:38.723
that has 10 employees or less

00:01:38.723 --> 00:01:40.824
that's in the industry
that you want to be in.

00:01:40.824 --> 00:01:43.087
It's a company that you look
up to and want to be like

00:01:43.087 --> 00:01:44.454
and aspire to learn from.

00:01:44.454 --> 00:01:45.625
And go work for them.

00:01:45.625 --> 00:01:47.671
And get as close to the
CEO/founder as possible.

00:01:47.671 --> 00:01:49.149
Learn, learn, learn, learn, learn.

00:01:49.149 --> 00:01:50.818
Take on as many projects as possible

00:01:50.818 --> 00:01:51.915
even though they're outside

00:01:51.915 --> 00:01:53.427
what you were specifically hired for

00:01:53.427 --> 00:01:56.580
so that when you go off
and start your own company

00:01:56.580 --> 00:01:58.334
or when you try to build that thing up

00:01:58.334 --> 00:02:00.616
you have all the tools, all the experience

00:02:00.616 --> 00:02:03.003
all the contacts necessary to do so.

00:02:03.003 --> 00:02:04.626
And so if you're not getting those tools

00:02:04.626 --> 00:02:06.528
experience and contacts
from your current job

00:02:06.528 --> 00:02:08.579
I'd look for a different job first.

00:02:08.579 --> 00:02:11.079
(hiphop beat)

00:02:12.106 --> 00:02:14.202
Number two is figure
out your business idea.

00:02:14.202 --> 00:02:15.822
So one of the great things about being

00:02:15.822 --> 00:02:17.145
in an industry that you love

00:02:17.145 --> 00:02:19.248
is you get to see how businesses work

00:02:19.248 --> 00:02:21.629
and you get to see where
the opportunities are.

00:02:21.629 --> 00:02:23.357
And so some of the great businesses

00:02:23.357 --> 00:02:25.620
have been founded by people
who are in an industry.

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:28.195
They had a job, they
were talking to customers

00:02:28.195 --> 00:02:29.889
and the customers that you were talking to

00:02:29.889 --> 00:02:33.574
their needs couldn't be
solved by the current company.

00:02:33.574 --> 00:02:36.717
And whenever you hear frustration
from your customer base

00:02:36.717 --> 00:02:38.772
and the company you're working at

00:02:38.772 --> 00:02:40.513
can't handle that situation

00:02:40.513 --> 00:02:42.037
that's an opportunity.

00:02:42.037 --> 00:02:43.810
You want to always be thinking to yourself

00:02:43.810 --> 00:02:45.028
"Is there something for me here?

00:02:45.028 --> 00:02:46.027
"Can I help this customer out?

00:02:46.027 --> 00:02:47.307
"Can I help them on the side?

00:02:47.307 --> 00:02:49.454
"Can I turn this into my
own business somehow?"

00:02:49.454 --> 00:02:51.068
When you're working in the industry

00:02:51.068 --> 00:02:53.743
you want to pay attention
to where the holes are.

00:02:53.743 --> 00:02:55.244
Where the market opportunities are.

00:02:55.244 --> 00:02:57.010
Where the paying points are.

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:59.346
And figure out what
your idea is going to be

00:02:59.346 --> 00:03:01.661
for a unique offering to the market.

00:03:01.661 --> 00:03:04.161
(hiphop beat)

00:03:05.235 --> 00:03:07.455
The number three thing to
do is figure out a plan.

00:03:07.455 --> 00:03:08.507
You need to have a plan.

00:03:08.507 --> 00:03:10.384
You need to think about
once you have your idea

00:03:10.384 --> 00:03:12.590
now how will you build
a business around it?

00:03:12.590 --> 00:03:14.158
How are you going to get new customers?

00:03:14.158 --> 00:03:15.373
How are you going to market yourself?

00:03:15.373 --> 00:03:17.416
How are you going to service the
customers that you're getting?

00:03:17.416 --> 00:03:19.726
How are you going to get
word-of-mouth marketing happening?

00:03:19.726 --> 00:03:21.509
What's your social media plan going to be?

00:03:21.509 --> 00:03:22.750
You start to have a plan.

00:03:22.750 --> 00:03:24.045
Now I understand the thing about planning.

00:03:24.045 --> 00:03:25.374
The plan is never going to be perfect.

00:03:25.374 --> 00:03:27.814
A lot of times people spend
too much time on the plan.

00:03:27.814 --> 00:03:29.343
They plan, they plan, they plan, they plan

00:03:29.343 --> 00:03:30.275
and they never do.

00:03:30.275 --> 00:03:32.371
That's not the solution either.

00:03:32.371 --> 00:03:33.881
But you don't want to just jump all in

00:03:33.881 --> 00:03:35.030
and not have a plan.

00:03:35.030 --> 00:03:36.977
Planning, even though as soon as you start

00:03:36.977 --> 00:03:39.239
actually being in business
your plan will change.

00:03:39.239 --> 00:03:41.440
It doesn't mean that the
planning process isn't valuable.

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:43.650
So you want to have a plan,
you want to do your research

00:03:43.650 --> 00:03:44.740
you want to get everything together

00:03:44.740 --> 00:03:46.376
and give yourself some confidence

00:03:46.376 --> 00:03:47.818
that this thing is going to work

00:03:47.818 --> 00:03:49.646
before just jumping all in on it.

00:03:49.646 --> 00:03:50.926
Basically you want to get to the point

00:03:50.926 --> 00:03:52.885
where if somebody
presented this thing to you

00:03:52.885 --> 00:03:54.466
you would want to invest in it.

00:03:54.466 --> 00:03:56.148
So this looks like a good plan.

00:03:56.148 --> 00:03:57.750
This looks like a good idea.

00:03:57.750 --> 00:04:00.396
Has that level of research
and detail gone into your plan

00:04:00.396 --> 00:04:01.478
to help you get to the point

00:04:01.478 --> 00:04:03.647
where you could comfortably
show it to somebody else

00:04:03.647 --> 00:04:05.788
and say, "That's a really good idea."

00:04:05.788 --> 00:04:08.624
(hiphop beat)

00:04:08.624 --> 00:04:09.894
For the number four tip

00:04:09.894 --> 00:04:11.845
I'm going to turn it
over to my friend Matthew

00:04:11.845 --> 00:04:14.610
from the Youtube channel, Trident Lion.

00:04:14.610 --> 00:04:15.806
- [Matthew] What's up Believe Nation?

00:04:15.806 --> 00:04:18.118
I'm Matthew, a.k.a Trident Lion

00:04:18.118 --> 00:04:19.840
from the Trident Lion channel.

00:04:19.840 --> 00:04:21.530
And tip number four is

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:24.363
quit your job with low or no risk.

00:04:25.197 --> 00:04:26.943
Not all entrepreneurs have the luxury

00:04:26.943 --> 00:04:31.479
and capability to take
and tolerate massive risk.

00:04:31.479 --> 00:04:33.014
Many of us, including myself

00:04:33.014 --> 00:04:36.097
have children we need to provide for.

00:04:36.981 --> 00:04:39.199
Hypothetically, it's better to jump ship

00:04:39.199 --> 00:04:43.007
by building a better ship while
you're on your current ship.

00:04:43.007 --> 00:04:45.516
Rather than jumping ship

00:04:45.516 --> 00:04:49.599
and trying to build a ship
while you're swimming.

00:04:50.562 --> 00:04:53.365
Imagine being able to leave your job

00:04:53.365 --> 00:04:56.061
quit with confidence and certainty.

00:04:56.061 --> 00:04:58.491
Quit with your next source of income

00:04:58.491 --> 00:05:01.241
being your entrepreneurial dream.

00:05:04.093 --> 00:05:05.978
The way to do this is to work.

00:05:05.978 --> 00:05:07.146
If you want it bad enough

00:05:07.146 --> 00:05:10.264
you have to put in the work after hours.

00:05:10.264 --> 00:05:12.562
I came across the
question a few years ago.

00:05:12.562 --> 00:05:16.603
The question of, "How do
you build a personal brand

00:05:16.603 --> 00:05:19.685
"And/or business while supporting a family

00:05:19.685 --> 00:05:21.685
"And working full time?"

00:05:22.748 --> 00:05:24.400
And one of the best answers I found

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:29.182
is the advice of one of my
and Evans virtual mentors.

00:05:29.182 --> 00:05:30.956
Gary Vaynerchuck.

00:05:30.956 --> 00:05:33.338
So for all of you entrepreneurs out there

00:05:33.338 --> 00:05:35.684
that cannot tolerate risk

00:05:35.684 --> 00:05:38.468
but still want to build
your entrepreneurial dream

00:05:38.468 --> 00:05:41.303
here is one powerful and effective way

00:05:41.303 --> 00:05:43.220
how to do exactly that.

00:05:47.125 --> 00:05:49.327
- So if you have a feel,
if you want to do it

00:05:49.327 --> 00:05:52.130
I don't want to hear about
this 9-5 bull (beep).

00:05:52.130 --> 00:05:52.963
What's that?

00:05:52.963 --> 00:05:53.796
- [Audience Member] I quit!

00:05:53.796 --> 00:05:54.629
- You quit?

00:05:54.629 --> 00:05:55.462
(laughs)

00:05:55.462 --> 00:05:56.362
I quit, nice.

00:05:56.362 --> 00:05:58.435
I don't want to hear about
this two job thing right?

00:05:58.435 --> 00:05:59.851
9-5, I don't have time.

00:05:59.851 --> 00:06:01.887
If you want this, if you're miserable

00:06:01.887 --> 00:06:02.733
or if you don't like it

00:06:02.733 --> 00:06:03.694
or you want to do something else

00:06:03.694 --> 00:06:04.992
and you have a passion somewhere else

00:06:04.992 --> 00:06:08.094
work 9-5, spend a couple
hours with your family.

00:06:08.094 --> 00:06:10.323
Seven to two in the
morning is plenty of time

00:06:10.323 --> 00:06:11.156
to do damage.

00:06:11.156 --> 00:06:13.057
(audience laughs)

00:06:13.057 --> 00:06:14.590
But that's it.

00:06:14.590 --> 00:06:18.307
It's not going to happen any other way.

00:06:18.307 --> 00:06:19.880
How do you get money to do what you love?

00:06:19.880 --> 00:06:21.335
You don't right?

00:06:21.335 --> 00:06:22.748
I lost a (beep) load of money

00:06:22.748 --> 00:06:24.560
when I started doing what I loved.

00:06:24.560 --> 00:06:27.306
What you do is you position
yourself to succeed.

00:06:27.306 --> 00:06:29.538
So for example, if you're
doing something else

00:06:29.538 --> 00:06:31.163
and you want to do this thing you love

00:06:31.163 --> 00:06:32.512
you do it after hours.

00:06:32.512 --> 00:06:35.134
You work 9-6, you get home.

00:06:35.134 --> 00:06:37.511
You kiss the dog, and you go to town.

00:06:37.511 --> 00:06:38.601
(audience laughs)

00:06:38.601 --> 00:06:39.434
Right?

00:06:39.434 --> 00:06:40.676
I mean, you start building
your equity and your brand

00:06:40.676 --> 00:06:42.879
and whatever you're trying
to accomplish, after hours.

00:06:42.879 --> 00:06:46.641
Everybody has time, stop
watching (beep) Lost.

00:06:46.641 --> 00:06:49.474
(audience laughs)

00:06:52.167 --> 00:06:53.582
- [Matthew] By putting in the work

00:06:53.582 --> 00:06:55.387
and being patient

00:06:55.387 --> 00:06:58.383
it is possible to turn
your entrepreneurial dream

00:06:58.383 --> 00:07:01.574
into your career with practically no risk.

00:07:01.574 --> 00:07:03.898
Quitting your job with certainty.

00:07:03.898 --> 00:07:06.305
If you want to quit your
job without the risk

00:07:06.305 --> 00:07:08.724
putting in the work towards
your entrepreneurial dream

00:07:08.724 --> 00:07:10.309
and being patient

00:07:10.309 --> 00:07:13.412
those are two important
things that you need to do

00:07:13.412 --> 00:07:14.659
before you quit.

00:07:14.659 --> 00:07:16.873
Realize if you have a busy schedule

00:07:16.873 --> 00:07:19.974
some of us, like I said have
a full time job and children.

00:07:19.974 --> 00:07:22.553
So dedicating time for
your entrepreneurial dream

00:07:22.553 --> 00:07:23.803
can be limited.

00:07:24.995 --> 00:07:27.530
Time efficiency and time effectiveness

00:07:27.530 --> 00:07:30.352
should be taken serious.

00:07:30.352 --> 00:07:32.290
You don't want to waste your limited time

00:07:32.290 --> 00:07:33.491
building an entrepreneurial dream

00:07:33.491 --> 00:07:35.241
on unimportant tasks.

00:07:37.314 --> 00:07:39.797
One great solution to this

00:07:39.797 --> 00:07:42.047
is to utilize Pareto's Law.

00:07:44.072 --> 00:07:46.774
Consider and ask yourself

00:07:46.774 --> 00:07:50.777
what is the most important 20% of the work

00:07:50.777 --> 00:07:53.921
that goes into building
my entrepreneurial dream

00:07:53.921 --> 00:07:57.007
for 80% of the outcome?

00:07:57.007 --> 00:07:58.304
If you want to quit your job

00:07:58.304 --> 00:08:01.275
to have a career doing
your entrepreneurial dream

00:08:01.275 --> 00:08:02.843
with little to no risk

00:08:02.843 --> 00:08:06.487
like Gary Vee has said, do it after hours.

00:08:06.487 --> 00:08:08.719
Put in the work, be
patient, be persistent.

00:08:08.719 --> 00:08:10.385
Learn as you go.

00:08:10.385 --> 00:08:11.865
Grow as you learn

00:08:11.865 --> 00:08:15.510
and be sure to never
quit on creating a life

00:08:15.510 --> 00:08:19.010
doing your personal entrepreneurial dream.

00:08:20.861 --> 00:08:22.848
So there you have the
number four thing to do

00:08:22.848 --> 00:08:24.931
before quitting your job.

00:08:28.620 --> 00:08:31.120
(hiphop beat)

00:08:32.230 --> 00:08:34.622
- My number five tip is run the numbers.

00:08:34.622 --> 00:08:36.834
So I think you should start at a company

00:08:36.834 --> 00:08:38.377
and then do your business on the side.

00:08:38.377 --> 00:08:39.671
And the point where you leave your job

00:08:39.671 --> 00:08:41.015
to go into your business full time

00:08:41.015 --> 00:08:43.354
is when you can make
enough from your business

00:08:43.354 --> 00:08:44.742
to pay off all your bills.

00:08:44.742 --> 00:08:47.563
So you need to know how much it costs you

00:08:47.563 --> 00:08:49.982
to live your life every month.

00:08:49.982 --> 00:08:51.344
And it doesn't have to
be a life of luxury.

00:08:51.344 --> 00:08:52.327
We're not talking about going out

00:08:52.327 --> 00:08:53.384
and buying expensive cars

00:08:53.384 --> 00:08:55.384
and going off on expensive trips.

00:08:55.384 --> 00:09:00.244
Just the basics, food,
internet, mortgage or rent.

00:09:00.244 --> 00:09:01.992
What does that equal every month

00:09:01.992 --> 00:09:03.687
so you know here's what I have to make

00:09:03.687 --> 00:09:06.639
from my business to survive.

00:09:06.639 --> 00:09:07.989
And if you can get to that point

00:09:07.989 --> 00:09:10.446
as a part time entrepreneur

00:09:10.446 --> 00:09:12.282
then you know, listen I could quit my job

00:09:12.282 --> 00:09:14.822
I could spend full time
now working on my business

00:09:14.822 --> 00:09:16.371
and I have enough to cover my basics.

00:09:16.371 --> 00:09:18.897
Now that I'm spending
more time on my business

00:09:18.897 --> 00:09:20.581
I can rapidly grow it up

00:09:20.581 --> 00:09:21.786
and earn more as well

00:09:21.786 --> 00:09:24.157
but you can't do that
until you know the numbers.

00:09:24.157 --> 00:09:25.833
So learn the numbers to know how much

00:09:25.833 --> 00:09:26.967
you need to survive

00:09:26.967 --> 00:09:28.790
and how much you're
making from your business.

00:09:28.790 --> 00:09:31.373
(hip-hop beat)

00:09:32.371 --> 00:09:34.454
So number six is then start on the side.

00:09:34.454 --> 00:09:35.692
We want to get started.

00:09:35.692 --> 00:09:38.219
Don't just have this idea
and do nothing about it.

00:09:38.219 --> 00:09:40.699
It's not just have a job
but learn about the industry

00:09:40.699 --> 00:09:43.077
and then wait for some
magical moment to start.

00:09:43.077 --> 00:09:44.172
No like, start now.

00:09:44.172 --> 00:09:46.451
Start on the side, start immediately.

00:09:46.451 --> 00:09:48.644
Weekends, evenings, we're going right away

00:09:48.644 --> 00:09:50.096
to try to build our business up.

00:09:50.096 --> 00:09:51.809
Even if it's free work at the start.

00:09:51.809 --> 00:09:52.956
Even if it's spec work

00:09:52.956 --> 00:09:54.468
just to build up your portfolio

00:09:54.468 --> 00:09:55.790
just to build up your experience

00:09:55.790 --> 00:09:57.398
just to build up the connections

00:09:57.398 --> 00:09:59.365
and understanding how the industry works.

00:09:59.365 --> 00:10:01.332
It's worth it on the side

00:10:01.332 --> 00:10:03.559
to start building some momentum

00:10:03.559 --> 00:10:04.715
because it's going to take a while

00:10:04.715 --> 00:10:06.404
to get your company off the ground.

00:10:06.404 --> 00:10:08.260
It's not just going to happen for you.

00:10:08.260 --> 00:10:10.377
And so, starting now

00:10:10.377 --> 00:10:12.031
starting and sucking right?

00:10:12.031 --> 00:10:14.624
Starting and improving,
slowly, slowly, slowly, slowly.

00:10:14.624 --> 00:10:16.162
Take everything that you
learned from your company

00:10:16.162 --> 00:10:17.453
that you have your job at

00:10:17.453 --> 00:10:19.317
and you're putting it
into your own business.

00:10:19.317 --> 00:10:20.383
Building that up.

00:10:20.383 --> 00:10:22.271
And not waiting, because too many people

00:10:22.271 --> 00:10:24.468
have these great ideas
while they're at a job

00:10:24.468 --> 00:10:25.723
and maybe the job sucks

00:10:25.723 --> 00:10:27.508
or maybe the job is great

00:10:27.508 --> 00:10:28.984
but you still just sit on the idea.

00:10:28.984 --> 00:10:30.799
You don't do anything with it.

00:10:30.799 --> 00:10:32.218
Well the key is to do something with it

00:10:32.218 --> 00:10:34.265
and the hardest part is,
you have this big vision

00:10:34.265 --> 00:10:35.693
for where you want to go

00:10:35.693 --> 00:10:37.491
and you know you can't do it right now.

00:10:37.491 --> 00:10:39.255
And a lot of people
just sit on the vision.

00:10:39.255 --> 00:10:40.608
They just sit on the idea.

00:10:40.608 --> 00:10:42.348
Well you stick to the big vision

00:10:42.348 --> 00:10:44.296
this is the big thing that we want to do

00:10:44.296 --> 00:10:45.215
that I want to build

00:10:45.215 --> 00:10:47.037
but I'm starting here.

00:10:47.037 --> 00:10:48.846
I'm going to take a step and another step

00:10:48.846 --> 00:10:50.505
and another step and another step.

00:10:50.505 --> 00:10:52.485
It's thinking big and acting small.

00:10:52.485 --> 00:10:56.192
Most people think big
and act zero, do nothing.

00:10:56.192 --> 00:10:58.945
So find a way to start today, immediately.

00:10:58.945 --> 00:11:01.484
Every single day you're
spending time on your business

00:11:01.484 --> 00:11:02.998
to move your idea forward.

00:11:02.998 --> 00:11:05.498
(hiphop beat)

00:11:06.524 --> 00:11:08.708
And then number seven is
hit your survival number.

00:11:08.708 --> 00:11:09.665
This is last step.

00:11:09.665 --> 00:11:11.470
Once you hit that survival number

00:11:11.470 --> 00:11:13.297
and you know here's what I need to live

00:11:13.297 --> 00:11:14.280
and I've hit it

00:11:14.280 --> 00:11:16.817
it's having the courage
to say, "I'm ready to go."

00:11:16.817 --> 00:11:18.146
You know, maybe taking a pay-cut

00:11:18.146 --> 00:11:21.357
I'm not making as much as I am
now with my combined salaries

00:11:21.357 --> 00:11:23.223
from my businesses and the job I have

00:11:23.223 --> 00:11:25.795
but this business is the thing
that you wanted to build.

00:11:25.795 --> 00:11:27.196
You've hit your survival number.

00:11:27.196 --> 00:11:29.482
It's having the courage to leave that job

00:11:29.482 --> 00:11:31.382
take all the time you spent there

00:11:31.382 --> 00:11:33.036
and pour it into your company

00:11:33.036 --> 00:11:34.905
and really build something
you can be proud of.

00:11:34.905 --> 00:11:36.045
So once you've hit that survival number

00:11:36.045 --> 00:11:38.545
you got to have the
courage to act, to do it.

00:11:38.545 --> 00:11:40.254
To take the leap, to jump.

00:11:40.254 --> 00:11:41.894
And to have the confidence that your thing

00:11:41.894 --> 00:11:43.257
is going to work out.

00:11:43.257 --> 00:11:44.669
So that's my take on the seven things

00:11:44.669 --> 00:11:46.722
that you need to do
before quitting your job.

00:11:46.722 --> 00:11:48.663
I'd love to know, what did you guys think?

00:11:48.663 --> 00:11:50.255
Which rule was your favorite?

00:11:50.255 --> 00:11:52.108
Do you have an eight,
nine, ten that you'd like

00:11:52.108 --> 00:11:53.086
to add to the list?

00:11:53.086 --> 00:11:54.509
Leave it down in the comments below

00:11:54.509 --> 00:11:56.142
and I'm going to join in the discussion.

00:11:56.142 --> 00:11:58.352
I also wanted to thank
Matthew from Trident Lion

00:11:58.352 --> 00:11:59.660
for his point number four

00:11:59.660 --> 00:12:01.731
as well Matthew picked
up a copy of my book

00:12:01.731 --> 00:12:04.151
Your One Word, and made
an awesome book review

00:12:04.151 --> 00:12:05.488
on his channel as well.

00:12:05.488 --> 00:12:07.205
So thank you Matthew for the love.

00:12:07.205 --> 00:12:08.660
I really, really appreciate it

00:12:08.660 --> 00:12:10.919
and I'm glad that you
enjoyed the book as well.

